boba fett is one of the most iconic  characters in the star wars universe he  might just be one man but he's been  played by over a dozen actors since a  character was first created think you  can name them all  before the release of the empire strikes  back or even the infamous holiday  special boba fett made its debut at an  annual fall parade in san anselmo  california on sunday september 24th  1978. san anselmo was home to 52 parkway  often known as george lucas's secret  lair which is why it was chosen as the  site of the beloved bounty hunter's  premiere assistant film editor dwayne  dunham wore the famous armor in the  parade simply because he was the right  size sure have him turn around and get a  shot of the  jetpack  you do it dwayne  according to dunham the parade took  place on an extremely hot day in san  auselmo which he recalled could have  been 100 degrees since no one knew who  his character was at the time few fans  approached him though dunham did in fact  sign autographs for this he even had to  ask a nearby producer gary kurtz if fett  had one tea in it or two  the first on-screen appearance of boba  fett came two months after the san  auselmo parade during the now notorious  star wars holiday special the bounty  hunter shows up in an animated sequence  in which he is voiced by don franks i  take it you have no love of the empire  after the millennium falcon crashes on a  water planet luke and the droids try to  rescue their friends as soon as they  land however they're threatened by a  large beast that phet fights off thus  gaining the hero's trust in truth he's  been sent by the empire to infiltrate  the rebels in the hopes of finding the  location of their base franks was a  canadian actor who worked regularly up  until his passing in 2016 at the age of  84. his most visible roles include  walter on the canadian tv series le  femme nikita and chief jake newby in the  1981 slasher classic my bloody valentine  most fans didn't get to meet boba fett  until he went on the hunt for han solo  and the empire strikes back for most of  boba fett's scenes in that movie and  return of the jedi the man in the suit  is jeremy bullock the english actor who  had appeared in multiple british tv  series and films before becoming part of  star wars but his silent role as boba  fett remains by far his most well  remembered speaking to io9 in 2011  bollocks said he never expected boba  fett's character to become so popular  when asked what he thought boba got up  to after plunging into the sarlacc pit  bullock suggested that boba might have  tracked down and killed mace windu who  killed boba's father in attack of the  clones before appearing to die one movie  later bullock continued to act on enough  in the decades after empire and even  made a cameo appearance in revenge of  the sith in december 2020 he died at the  age of 75 from complications of  parkinson's disease  jeremy bollock's face only appears once  strong the empire strikes back and it  isn't while he's playing boba when luke  skywalker infiltrates bespin's cloud  city leia spots him and warns that he's  falling into a trap at the same time an  imperial officer is trying to pull her  away that officer is lieutenant shekel  played by bullock the production  shooting schedules conflicted at the  time however and in order to shoot that  scene bullock couldn't play boba fett in  another one in which the bounty hunter  walks down a hallway with vader lando  and lobot so john morton got to be boba  fett for that one scene that isn't  morton's only role in empire either he  also played rebel pilot dark ralter luke  skywalker's gunner during the battle of  huff having previously worked as a  stuntman morton didn't do much more  acting after his career although he did  score smaller roles in two other sci-fi  classics released the same year as  empire flash gordon and superman 2.  while jeremy bullock and john morton  played the physical role of boba fett in  the original star wars trilogy the voice  fans initially heard coming out of  fett's helmet was that of jason wingreen  what if he doesn't survive he's worth a  lot to me  this isn't the case for many modern star  wars fans however as the 2004 dvd  releases swapped to win green's voice  with tim wearer morrisons what if he  doesn't survive he's worth a lot to me  when green claimed that for him  portraying boba fett took no more than  10 minutes of work there's an argument  to be made that win green wasn't treated  very fairly by the star wars franchise  after lending his voice to the famous  bounty hunter his name wasn't included  and the credits of empire strikes back  and his involvement wasn't even public  knowledge until around the year 2000  most shockingly he never received any  residual compensation for his work even  though his voice was used for boba fett  action figures when green died on  christmas day 2015 he was 95 years old  back in 1981 george lucas sold the radio  rights for the original star wars  trilogy to npr for the whopping sum of  one dollar the filmmaker had been  listening to nbr since his college days  and was inclined to feel generous  towards them all three movies were  eventually adapted into radio dramas  split into half hour long installments  certain actors from the movies reprised  their roles but most of the other  characters had to be recast including  boba fett in the 1983 empire strikes  back radio play boba fett was played by  alan rosenberg an actor who has worked  steadily since the late 1970s mostly in  television unfortunately by the time a  return of the jedi adaptation could be  made federal funding cuts and a number  of other factors had put the radio play  on hold it wasn't until 1996 that the  six-part drama was recorded with ed  bagley jr taking over the role of boba  fett around the same time in 1994 the  popular dark empire comic book series  was adapted into two audio dramas for  the role of boba fett character actor  joseph hacker was chosen packer has  appeared on dozens of tv shows over the  years from quantum leap to 24. the final  actor to play phet in an audio drama was  the otherwise unknown tim glovatsky who  played the bounty hunter in dark forces  rebel agent an adaptation of the novel  of the same name  when the special edition of a new hope  hit theaters in 1997 it included an  uncompleted scene from the original  production in which jabba the hurt and  han solo talk before the falcon leaves  tatooine along with a group of armed  henchmen jabba is accompanied by the  silent but intimidating figure of boba  fett the bounty hunter was worked into  the story digitally courtesy of  industrial light and magic animator mark  austin who dons the iconic armor for the  scene while his appearance is brief in a  new hope austin obviously feels attached  to the role he even played the bounty  hunter for a second time on the boba  fett fan club's web series no  disintegrations these episodes are meant  to be transmissions from boba fett's  ship most of which take place within  specific chapters of the saga  when it came time to produce a special  edition of return of the jedi george  lucas apparently wanted more boba fett  even though he never did manage to work  in an escape from the sarlacc pit what  fans do get however is more time with  the armored bounty hunter dronie  extended song and dance number in jabba  the hutt's palace for most of these new  boba fett shots special effects artists  don bees stepped into the character's  iconic armor nelson hall another vfx  artist provided the rest of the footage  for fete in a 2016 interview with  starwars.com bees revealed he also  played a musician in jabba's band as  well as a whole bunch of stormtroopers  and imperial officers in a new hope  apparently he and nelson hall stuck  themselves in so many scenes that their  effects supervisor actually had to ask  them to tone it down  if you're a fan of animated star wars  properties you've likely heard tom  kane's voice he's a narrator of star  wars the clone wars as well as the voice  of yoda in that series and a number of  other productions as far as boba fett is  concerned however kane has portrayed the  bounty hunter three times albeit only in  star wars video games kane's first  outing as boba fett came during 2000  star wars demolition a game in which  players put different vehicles from the  franchise against each other kane voice  fed once again in a 2001 real-time  strategy game star wars galactic  battlegrounds finally he played fett in  2003's star wars jedi knight jedi  academy which has a particularly special  place in many fans hearts  boba fett this doesn't concern you jedi  just walk away  attack of the clones reveals a whole lot  about boba fett first it's shown that  the bounty hunter is a clone created as  payment to jango fett by the clone  makers of camino in exchange for the use  of his dna to create their clone army  the movie also makes clear that boba  fett's appreciation of violence emerged  at a young age finally it's revealed  that fett saw his father die on geonosis  and mace windu's hands the image of  young boba fett holding django's helmet  is one of the most memorable of the  prequel trilogy younger boba fett is  played by the new zealand-born actor  daniel logan playing boba fett left an  interesting mark on the young performer  too when looper spoke to him in april  2020 he revealed that like jake lloyd he  suffered plenty of bullying for his role  in the trilogy he said i think we're  very very blessed that we came in during  the era right before social media and  this whole entire internet explosion  because i think it could have turned out  worse luckily this hasn't stopped him  embracing his connection with the star  wars saga and when logan got the call to  a prizes role in the clone wars he  pretty much jumped at the opportunity  in 1998 lucasarts and nintendo teamed up  to release the flight action game star  wars rogue squadron in this game the  player guides the eponymous rebel group  through a variety of mission objectives  it proved popular enough to spawn two  sequels including 2003's star wars rogue  squadron 3 rebel strike actor chris cox  played multiple characters in rebel  strike including boba fett his fed  performance are spotlighted by a mission  that recreates leia's futile pursuit of  the bounty hunter when he leaves best  bin with the frozen han solo while rebel  strike is the only game in which cox  portrayed boba fett is only one of many  star wars games he's worked on the  prolific voice actor can be heard across  the star wars galaxy from fallen order  to battlefront to the force unleashed  well fans in his home country of new  zealand were already familiar with his  work before he stepped into the star  wars universe it was timera morrison's  pitch perfect performance as jango fett  an attack of the clones that made him  known to audiences around the world  since that film establishes that boba is  a clone of django it also laid the  foundation for morrison to soften the  disappointment so many fans suffered in  return of the jedi by finally returning  boba fett to the land of the living  blues happening  morrison voiced boba fett a number of  times before he played him in a  live-action capacity though when the  special editions of the original trilogy  got new home releases in 2004 jason  wingreen's voice was replaced with  morrisons morrison went on to voice the  character in a number of video games  including 2005's battlefront 2 and  2006's empire at war more recently in  the second season of the mandalorian  morrison's boba fett joins up with din  jaren to help rescue grogu from the  clutches of moff gideon try saying that  six times that season ended with the  revelation that phet will be getting his  own solo series on disney plus in  december 2021  d bradley baker has enjoyed a long  varied and incredibly successful voice  acting career including a whole lot of  work in the star wars universe he's  perhaps best known for voicing captain  rex and the clone wars rebels and the  bad batch though he also played a number  of clone troopers in each series baker  portrayed boba fett in both of the force  unleashed games too in 2011 the year  after force unleash 2 was released fans  were able to hear him voice a bounty  hunter once again albeit as part of a  very different production that year  disney's hollywood studios debuted star  tours the adventures continue an  attraction that sees baker reprises role  as the galaxy's most dangerous bounty  hunter  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the second season of the mandalorian  where morrison's boba fett joins up with  dinjarin to help rescue grogu from the  clutches of moff gideon seriously guys  come on subscribe to our youtube channel  and to the bell so you don't miss a  single one

